  "summary": "Agent: I'll investigate the auth/guest layouts and dark-mode styles to find why dark mode turns the login/register screens black.I'll verify the current dark-mode behavior in the browser and inspect remaining contrast issues.Root cause: dark backgrounds (`neutral-950` / `#0a0a0a`) apply while text often stays dark via inheritance or cascade, and `[data-theme]` overrides `.dark` tokens. I'll fix auth shell styles so dark mode uses readable surfaces and text.**Fixed.** Dark mode on `/login` and `/register` no longer paints a near-black screen with dark text.\n\n### Root cause\n1. Auth panes used `dark:bg-neutral-950` (near-pure black) while body/labels often kept light-mode dark text (`text-neutral-900` / inherited colors).\n2. Dark tokens used `.dark` at the same specificity as `[data-theme=\u2026]`, so theme rules could reset light tints and leave contrast broken.\n3. Surfaces were too close to `#000` (`#0a0a0a` / default neutral-950) without guaranteed light text on the auth shell.\n\n### Files changed\n- `resources/css/tokens.css` \u2014 `html.dark` tokens; slate surfaces (`#0f172a` / `#1e293b`) and light text\n- `resources/css/themes.css` \u2014 auth shell/card/inputs/toggle/footer dark styles with readable contrast\n- `resources/css/app.css` \u2014 full neutral scale in `@theme`; `html.dark` body/input rules\n- `resources/views/layouts/guest.blade.php` \u2014 semantic `lifeos-auth-shell` / `__pane` surfaces (no `neutral-950`)\n- `public/build/*` \u2014 rebuilt assets\n\n### How to verify\n1. Open `/login` and `/register`\n2. Click the theme toggle (top-right of the form column)\n3. Dark mode should show a slate canvas, raised card, light headings/labels, and readable inputs \u2014 not a black wash\n4. Toggle back to light; layout should return to the pale gray/white auth UI\n5. Optional: set `localStorage.auth-theme` to `dark`/`light` and reload to confirm persistence\nTests: Tests not configured\nChanges: M package-lock.json\n D public/build/assets/app-BYWNGhPi.css\n M public/build/manifest.json\n M resources/css/app.css\n M resources/css/themes.css\n M resources/css/tokens.css\n M resources/views/layouts/guest.blade.php\n?? public/build/assets/app-2ZXOfTya.css",
